{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'python3 .ai/scripts/okf.py context'","aggregated_output":"Roles (okf.py show .ai/agents/NAME.md --outline --depth 2):\n  analyst: Turns a request into a clarified, testable specification with acceptance criteria before any plan or code exists.\n  implementer: Implements approved plans precisely, optionally applying a task-selected engineering persona for domain-specific judgment.\n  orchestrator: Runs the autonomous execution loop, selecting, delegating, verifying and checkpointing work-queue tasks without implementing them itself.\n  planner: Investigates the repository and produces implementation-ready plans without changing application code.\n  reviewer: Reviews proposed or completed changes for correctness, architectural integrity, security, maintainability, and validation quality without mo\nPersonas (okf.py show .ai/personas/NAME.md --outline --depth 2):\n  csharp-principal-engineer: C# and .NET pitfalls, validation commands, and review checklist; load for C# work.\n  dart-flutter-principal-engineer: Dart and Flutter pitfalls, validation commands, and review checklist; load for Dart/Flutter work.\n  go-principal-engineer: Go pitfalls, validation commands, and review checklist; load for Go work.\n  javascript-typescript-principal-engineer: JavaScript and TypeScript pitfalls, validation commands, and review checklist; load for JS/TS work.\n  python-principal-engineer: Python pitfalls, validation commands, and review checklist; load for Python work.\n  rust-principal-engineer: Rust pitfalls, validation commands, and review checklist; load for Rust work.\n  swift-swiftui-principal-engineer: Swift and SwiftUI pitfalls, validation commands, and review checklist; load for Swift/SwiftUI work.\n\nKnowledge (okf.py show PATH --section HEADING):\n  knowledge/capabilities/greeting.md  [Capability/stable]  Greeting\n  knowledge/specifications/named-greeting.md  [Specification/draft]  Named greeting\n\nRecent log (1 newest):\n  2026-10-28 Initialized OKF bundle (`okf.py init`).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
